        "original_id": "d7af856a-c9ea-53b2-8881-d40edaa1fcf4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Columbia University, University of Colorado system\n- Places: Upper Manhattan, New York City, Colorado, Denver, Aurora\n- People: Robert Cunningham Humphreys, Kurt Alme, Charles C. Lovell\n- Roles: student, graduate, law clerk\n- Topics: universities, higher education\n\nFacts:\n- Columbia University was established in 1754 as a private Ivy League research university in Upper Manhattan, New York City.\n- Columbia University is often cited as one of the world's most prestigious universities.\n- Robert Cunningham Humphreys was a student at Columbia University from 1926 to 1927.\n- The University of Colorado system consists of four public university campuses in Colorado.\n- The University of Colorado system includes the University of Colorado Boulder, the University of Colorado Colorado Springs, the University of Colorado Denver in downtown Denver, and the Anschutz Medical Campus in Aurora.\n- Kurt Alme graduated from the University of Colorado and Harvard Law School.\n- Kurt Alme clerked for Charles C. Lovell of the United States District Court for the District of Montana.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
